          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: cōnfestim",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cōnfestim — \"at once, without delay\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Dux, ubi nūntium audīvit, cōnfestim mīlitēs mīsit. When the leader heard the news, he sent soldiers at once."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Common in Caesar and Livy for a swift reaction: one thing heard, the next done."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cōnfestim is linked by Lewis & Short with festīnō, \"to hurry\" (taught), with the prefix con-: all in a rush. The exact formation is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
