          "title": "You'll want to know: prōtinus",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "prōtinus — \"immediately; straight on\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ē raedā dēscendit et prōtinus domum festīnāvit. He got down from the carriage and hurried straight home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First in space, 'onward, straight ahead'; then in time, 'at once'. Both senses are classical."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "prōtinus is built on prō, \"forward\", and tenus, \"as far as\" (Lewis & Short): onward, and then without a break."
            }
          ]
        },
